  "question": {
    "text": "If $\\quad \\lim _{x \\rightarrow 1^{+}} \\frac{(x-1)(6+\\lambda \\cos (x-1))+\\mu \\sin (1-x)}{(x-1)^3}=-1$, where $\\lambda, \\mu \\in \\mathbb{R}$, then $\\lambda+\\mu$ is equal to"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "18",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "20",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "19",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "17",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\text { Put } x=1+h \\\\ & \\lim _{h \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{h(6+\\lambda \\cosh )-\\mu \\sinh }{h^3}=-1 \\\\ & \\lim _{h \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{h\\left(6+\\lambda\\left(1-\\frac{h^2}{2!}\\right)\\right)-\\mu\\left(h-\\frac{h^3}{3!}\\right)}{h^3}=-1 \\\\ & 6+\\lambda-\\mu=0 \\text { and }-\\frac{\\lambda}{2}+\\frac{\\mu}{6}=-1 \\\\ & \\lambda+\\mu=18\\end{aligned}$"
  }
